issue.body:
## Versions

`vize` **0.593.0** (npm), Node 26.6.0, macOS arm64. (First noted in a comment on #7208, which was closed for the
other two parts.)

## Reproduction

Repro directory: `repro/xf-composable-provide/`.

`src/composables/selection.ts`

```ts
import { ref } from "vue";
import type { InjectionKey, Ref } from "vue";

export const SelectedKey: InjectionKey<Ref<string[]>> = Symbol("selected");
export const ToastKey: InjectionKey<{ message: Ref<string>; show(text: string): void }> =
  Symbol("toast");

export function useSelection(): { selected: Ref<string[]>; clear(): void } {
  const selected = ref<string[]>([]);
  return { selected, clear: () => (selected.value = []) };
}

export function useToast(): { message: Ref<string>; show(text: string): void } {
  const message = ref("");
  return { message, show: text => (message.value = text) };
}
```

`src/App.vue`

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { provide } from "vue";
import { SelectedKey, ToastKey, useSelection, useToast } from "./composables/selection";
import Picker from "./components/Picker.vue";

// a ref returned by a composable
const { selected } = useSelection();
provide(SelectedKey, selected);

// an object of refs and functions returned by a composable
const toast = useToast();
provide(ToastKey, toast);
</script>

<template>
  <Picker />
</template>
```

`src/components/Picker.vue`

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { inject } from "vue";
import { SelectedKey, ToastKey } from "../composables/selection";

const selected = inject(SelectedKey)!;
const toast = inject(ToastKey)!;
</script>

<template>
  <button type="button" @click="toast.show(selected.join(', '))">{{ toast.message.value }}</button>
</template>
```

```
$ vize lint -f plain --no-config --cross-file "src/**/*.vue"
  src/App.vue:8:1 warning cross-file vize:croquis/cf/non-reactive-provide: provide('SelectedKey') value is not reactive - consumers won't see updates
  src/App.vue:12:1 warning cross-file vize:croquis/cf/non-reactive-provide: provide('ToastKey') value is not reactive - consumers won't see updates
```

## Expected

No findings. `selected` is the `ref` created in `useSelection()`; `toast` is a plain object whose `message` is a ref and
whose functions write to it, so consumers do see updates. Both values are typed `Ref<…>` / `{ message: Ref<string> }`
by the composables' return types and by the keys.

If following the composable is out of scope, a value whose origin is unknown (a call result) should not be reported as
"not reactive" — only values that are known to be plain (literals, `const x = 1`, a `.value` read) should.

Related: #10901 (the same rule, a different shape: a type assertion there, a composable return value here).

